      "writtenOn": "2024-04-29T15:09:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The thing is that the opaque vendor part of the capabilities might encode some information about the multiplexing capability of the remote device. Imagine a banded headphones (single device) with supported audio locations in PAC service set to `Left | Right`. The BT stack would set a single sink requirement with the audio allocation set to `Left | Right`, but the vendor config provider could\ncheck the multiplexing capability of the remote (by interpreting the vendor capabilities) and decide whether to provide a single ASE configuration with `Left|Right` allocation (multiplexing) or two Ase configurations, one with `Left` and the other with `Right` (no multiplexing). I think that all the required locations should be get their configurations, but not necessarily in a single ASE configuration.",
      "parentUuid": "64308ec7_99c13676",
      "revId": "6d882e30ace912a5ef9afd619b8d711d04b05a22",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
